INT. FROZEN FOOD WAREHOUSE, WALK-IN FREEZER - NIGHT

Minus twenty. Breath clouds. Pallets of frozen pierogi stacked to the rafters.

DELPHINE KOWALCZYK-ABARA (30s, parka, safecracker's fingertips) kneels at a steel floor safe. Stethoscope on the dial.

Click. Click. Click.

She stops. Listens. Click.

The heavy door groans. TOBIAS "TOBY" FENWICK (20s, lookout, ski mask rolled up) slips in, hopping from foot to foot.

TOBY
My toes are gone.

DELPHINE
You've got more.

TOBY
How long?

DELPHINE
Quiet.

Click.

TOBY
This is going well.

DELPHINE
It's going fine.

TOBY
Too well. Nobody's here.

DELPHINE
Nobody's here because it's a freezer.

She turns the dial. The safe door swings open. Inside, empty. Just a single index card.

DELPHINE (CONT'D)
(reading)
"Sorry. -- Management."

TOBY
They knew!

DELPHINE ^
They knew.

The freezer lights snap off. Dark. Then back on, bright. The heavy door is closed.

Outside, a latch clicks. A padlock.

TOBY
Delphine?

DELPHINE
Don't.

TOBY
We're locked in.

DELPHINE
I said don't.

She pockets the card. Pulls her hood tight. Looks up at the pierogi.

DELPHINE (CONT'D)
At least we won't starve.
